                            SCP-4273
                        </div>
                    

                    

                    



                    <div id="page-content">
                        

<div style="text-align: right;"><div class="page-rate-widget-box"><span class="rate-points">rating:&nbsp;<span class="number prw54353">-10</span></span><span class="rateup btn btn-default"><a title="I like it" href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.modules.PageRateWidgetModule.listeners.rate(event, 1)">+</a></span><span class="ratedown btn btn-default"><a title="I don't like it" href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.modules.PageRateWidgetModule.listeners.rate(event, -1)">&#8211;</a></span><span class="cancel btn btn-default"><a title="Cancel my vote" href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.modules.PageRateWidgetModule.listeners.cancelVote(event)">x</a></span></div></div>
<p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-XXXX</p>
<p><strong>Object Class:</strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Safe</span> Euclid</p>
<p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-XXXX is to be kept at Site-95, in a standard size anomalous vehicle containment bay with all surfaces covered in blast-resistant plating.</p>
<p>Every 6-7 months SCP-XXXX is to be checked for maintenance issues. Should there be issues with any of its components, they are to be fixed as soon as possible to avoid any risk of SCP-XXXX becoming unstable. Under no circumstances is SCP-XXXX to be allowed to <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">activate its weaponry</span> be activated unless in a controlled and prepared testing environment approved by site command.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-1')">1</a></sup></p>
<p>Should SCP-XXXX endure massive amounts of physical damage during testing or field use, it is to be put in between Tesla coils approved by Level-3 engineers until its self-repair protocol is complete. <span style="color: blue">In accordance with Event-XXXX-4-CB, every 25th of December SCP-XXXX is to be immediatly incapacitated via the C4 package in the middle of the chamber. SCP-XXXX will be allowed to activate repair protocols after the 27th of December, and the C4 package replaced.</span></p>
<p>Should SCP-XXXX enter an unstable state as indicated by the sudden rapid vibration of SCP-XXXX, the blast doors leading to the entrance of its containment bay are to be closed immediately. The blast doors are to be kept closed for approximately thirty to forty minutes until all signs of the anomalous heat cease, at which point cleanup and maintenance is to commence. SCP-XXXX is to be handled with caution for the next 24 hours after said event.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX-1 is currently kept in a standard anomaly locker. SCP-XXXX-1 is only to be used in testing and field usage by personnel with the requirements for a bonding procedure. Personnel are to rotate shifts to avoid a potential containment breach.</p>
<p>In the event that any SCP-XXXX instance is encountered outside of containment, MTF-Epsilon-212 “Dragon Riders” is to be immediately dispatched to contain or terminate the instance, depending on the current situation. <span style="color: blue">In accordance with Event-XXXX-4-CB, MTF-Epsilon-212 is to report to site-95 as a precaution.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-2')">2</a></sup></span></p>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-XXXX is a black Mack Titan semi-truck, weighing approximately 125 tonnes. SCP-XXXX has been observed accelerating towards 240&#160;km/h within 2 seconds, despite not facilitating the engine power necessary to achieve said speeds[<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-3')">3</a></sup> This has also allowed SCP-XXXXX to be extremely resistant to physical damage, as several tests and incidents have shown SCP-XXXX being left as rusted and crumpled, yet completely immune to further harm of the SCP. See <strong>Addendum:Event-XXXX-4-CB</strong> for more details.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX is shown to have a self-repair protocol, which is only observed when SCP-XXXX is exposed to any source of electricity with high voltage. The exact method of this protocol's activation is unknown, but the hood of SCP-XXXX will open, and a pair of conjoined jumper cables attached to any source of electricity. If the source is out of reach, the cables will act as a conductor, causing the source to emit an unknown form of energy that has been described as “Pure electricity”, although the exact nature of this energy has yet to be studied extensively due to the longevity of the protocol.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-4')">4</a></sup></p>
<p>SCP-XXXX’s <span style="color: blue">former</span> most notable property, however, is the vast amount of weaponry and components stored in different areas of SCP-XXXX’s body, as most should not be able to fit inside of SCP-XXXX due to the size of several of the weapons.</p>
<p>A list of these weapons and components with locations and activation methods has been documented.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>NOTE:</strong> Personnel assigned to SCP-XXXX that attempt or request any further attempts into studying and understanding SCP-XXXX are required to view the list to become familiar with the components. Personnel not assigned to SCP-XXXX are not required to view the list.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;View&nbsp;armaments</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;hide&nbsp;armaments&nbsp;</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p><span style="font-size:0.8em;">Yes we are indeed aware that this list is rather pointless. No, we will not remove it as the latest breach has led to the creation of this list so we may be better prepared for a potential containment breach. -Dr. Sparks</span></p>
</blockquote>
<table class="wiki-content-table">
<tr>
<th>Weapon/Component identification</th>
<th>Location</th>
<th>Mode of activation</th>
<th>Additional notes</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>2 Breda-SAFATs</td>
<td>Hidden in the front fenders having a visible belt with HEAT type ammunition.</td>
<td>Two buttons on the sides of the steering wheel.</td>
<td>All attempts of removing the belt from the side of the gun have proved fruitless.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Quad barrel ZPU</td>
<td>Hidden within the roof of SCP-XXXX.</td>
<td>A switch located on the dashboard.</td>
<td>While it has no visible ammunition, it fires what appears to be HEAT type bullets, capable of penetrating most metals and exploding upon contact.</td>
</tr>
