<td>Several standard vehicle components such as the gas tank, speedometer, and even the rearview mirror are completely disconnected, non-functional, and even completely removed, testing ongoing.</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><span style="color: blue">SCP-XXXX is Autonomous to an unknown degree. SCP-XXXX mainly will display minor signs of self imposed movement, such as rotating to face the entrance to it’s containment chamber. On the 25th of December, SCP will instead activate automatically. As of Event-XXXX-4-CB, all activations have shown the same behavior. SCP-XXXX will attempt to cause intense damage to the area it is currently located in. Interestingly, SCP-XXXX will avoid harming anything related to Christmas.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-5" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-5')">5</a></sup></span></p>
<p>The vehicle’s ignition key, designated as SCP-XXXX-1 is constructed in a highly unusual fashion. It is currently the only object that activates both its engine, and its weapons, and is considered the most valuable component of SCP-XXXX.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX-1 can only be used by personnel who meet specific requirements.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-6" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-6')">6</a></sup> Any other personnel who attempt to use SCP-XXXX-1 to start SCP-XXXX will not cause any effect other than SCP-XXXX to refuse to start. However, it should be noted that if this is continuously tried for more than 5 attempts, SCP-XXXX will enter a destabilization state, at which point the engine will proceed to emit highly lethal amounts of carbon monoxide in a thick cloud, covering at least 2 miles in diameter in less than 2 minutes before igniting, killing any life form within its presence.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-7" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-7')">7</a></sup></p>
<p>SCP-XXXX-2 refers to any trailer attached to SCP-XXXX. Trailers will gain anomalous properties once attached to SCP-XXXX, all having varying properties depending on the attachment, yet some have been found to have constant properties, namely the growth of barbed and razor wire along any edges on the outside of the vehicle.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Attempts to find any potential individuals responsible for SCP-XXXX are underway.</span><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-8" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-8')">8</a></sup></p>
<p><strong>Addendum:</strong> Recovery log and After-Incident-Report-XXXX-RC<br />
SCP-XXXX was recovered from a small town in El Paso, Texas, where a local demolition derby was being held. Doctor Sparks, who was on vacation at the time, witnessed SCP-XXXX’s effects when an attack by local drug cartels attempted to storm the area, presumably to kill several workers seeing as how later investigation revealed drug usage, though SCP-XXXX was used to successfully terminate all attackers. However, the driver and previous possessor of SCP-XXXX-1 was fatally shot during the event. Dr. Sparks attempted to aid the driver, who instructed them to take SCP-XXXX and let it run free before expiring. SCP-XXXX was secured and contained, and the remaining survivors were given Class C amnestics. See after-incident-report for more information.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;interview&nbsp;log</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Collapse&nbsp;interview&nbsp;log</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Interviewed:</strong>Subject-█ a survivor of the incident, the manager of the event.</p>
<p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Doctor Sparks</p>
<p><strong>Foreword:</strong>Interrogation of Subject-█ after recovery of SCP-XXXX.</p>
<p><strong>&lt;Begin Log&gt;</strong></p>
<p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> Are you aware of why you are here?</p>
<p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> Not exactly, but if I had to take a guess, I’d say it's because of what happened earlier?</p>
<p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> Where Was the truck found exactly?</p>
<p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> You mean the Titan?</p>
<p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> Yes, do you know how it got there?</p>
<p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> I don’t know man, it just showed up, key and all.</p>
<p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> You mean to say that SCP-XXXX just showed up out of thin air?</p>
<p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> I mean, kind of. It just showed up one day, we tried it out and next thing we knew, we had a new attraction for the show, I mean we weren't about to let this pass up. You don’t just get a gift and question where it came from. Plus, a few months ago, we were running low on cash.<br />
<strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> You mean you all could operate SCP-XXXX without any trouble?</p>
<p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> Technically no. Seeing how big a hippy ███ was, it just wouldn’t start, even when he tried to hotwire it. Heck, when ███████ decided to become a medical doctor, the truck wouldn't start until he got drunk and even then it seemed to stop sometimes like he was trying to fight back against his inner rage.</p>
<p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> You mean to tell me that SCP-XXXX will not respond to anyone with good intentions?</p>
<p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> Two things. One, terrible nickname for it, just wanted to point that out. Two, actually no, it just worked for any one of us who just liked to live a little, have an adrenaline rush, enjoy high octane action, that kind of stuff. Look, basically as long as we didn't give a crap for our safety or others, we could drive it no problem<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-9" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-9')">9</a></sup> Or at least that's how I was told why the thing wouldn't budge when I tried to drive it. I've driven some of the most complex things with no sweat, but this just caused my head to spin. That or it didn’t like me. Either way, I guess that's how ██████ was able to drive that thing with no problem.</p>
<p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong> I see. Was the attack by that gang-related to SCP-XXXX in any way?</p>
<p><strong>Subject-█:</strong> Not really, I mean one of them did notice it and tried to get in before ██████ knocked ‘em out and got in and just annihilated them! Funny thing is, she was supposed to go up next for her performance with<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-10" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-10')">10</a></sup>, as you call it,spc-xxxx?</p>
<p><strong>Doctor Sparks:</strong>Close. While we also found that you had several workers who were in touch with the gang, are you sure no other motives were the cause for the attack? Like a rivalry or territory violation?</p>
<p><strong>Subject-█:</strong>No, I told them to get sober, obviously they didn’t, had to pay a huge debt, decided to give our tour a bad name, trashed everything, and now we're here. Honestly, this is the second biggest mishap we have had in the derby's history. Now can I please go? You know, I still have this thing to run. We’re putting on a christmas special soon, and it’s gonna be the big reveal!</p>
<p><strong>&lt;End Log&gt;</strong></p>
<p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> After the events of the interview, Subject was given class-c amnestics, and investigation of the location the event was held at, several narcotics were found, as well as a contact list related to the cartel involved in the incident, along with a schedule list, and plans for upcoming events, most of which were to involve SCP-XXXX.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Shortly after the initial containment of SCP-XXXX, a small torn business card was found in the glove compartment of SCP-XXXX, with text reading “Renex Industries”<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-11" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-11')">11</a></sup> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Current speculation suggests that SCP-XXXX is a product of this company, but no evidence has been found, other than the card itself, about this organization's existence</span><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-12" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-12')">12</a></sup></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Addendum-XXXX-T2:</strong> The following is a partial log detailing tests conducted on SCP-XXXX to find any additional anomalous properties should a trailer be attached. The tests shown are the most noticeable in changes in trailer properties and appearances, as most are repetitive and do not seem to change other than the growth of barbed and razor wire on the sides of the trailers.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-13" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-13')">13</a></sup></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;testing&nbsp;log</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Collapse&nbsp;testing&nbsp;log</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Test C</strong>- Date██/██/██</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Subject:</strong> SCP-XXXX, one tank trailer, primarily used for transporting gasoline.</p>
<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> The Trailer car was successfully attached to SCP-XXXX without incident. The tank was loaded with gasoline beforehand.</p>
<p><strong>Results:</strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">No noticeable differences other than barbed wire “growths”</span> the entire holding tank was composed of several layers of Lead, Titanium, and Cobalt, all of which are not used in such vehicles. Its weight remained the same. The gasoline appeared to be mildly corrosive.</p>
<p><strong>Notes:</strong> It appears that SCP-XXXX changed the trailer to either hold a more aggressive substance or to withstand potential damage dealt in case of an emergency. This may be useful if SCP-XXXX is approved for field use, as there are quite a few hostile substances we've encountered over the years.-Sparks</p>
</blockquote>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Test J</strong>- Date██/██/██</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Subject:</strong> SCP-XXXX, one field artillery cannon.<br />
<strong>Procedure:</strong> The field artillery cannon was attached to the truck after security personnel were able to goad D-2001 into operating SCP-XXXX. The artillery cannon was not armed.<br />
<strong>Results:</strong> The artillery cannon displayed signs of sentiance, and attempted to move and drag SCP-XXXX as it headed towards the exit area of testing zone-23. The artillery cannon was capable of producing a variety of sounds, metallic and equine in nature. The cannon fired three rounds before being detached from SCP-XXXX, where it ceased all movement.<br />
<strong>Notes:</strong> Because of this event, all trailer attachments involving weapons or objects that could be used as weapons are prohibited from testing until more information about SCP-XXXX can be found.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Test K</strong>- Date██/██/██</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Subject:</strong> SCP-XXXX, one horse trailer<br />
<strong>Procedure:</strong> The Trailer car was successfully attached to SCP-XXXX without incident. A domestic horse was loaded into the trailer beforehand.</p>
<p><strong>Results:</strong> After about 5 seconds after being attached, the trailer started shaking violently. Upon opening the doors, an unusually large wild horse<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-14" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-14')">14</a></sup>, resembling the domestic horse from before, ran out and bit several agents while bucking frantically. It was eventually sedated via injection from 3 horse tranquilizers. The subject was eventually released into the wild after confirmation that the horse did not show any other signs of anomalous properties and was deemed safe for release.</p>
<p><strong>Notes:</strong> Along with the recent information gathered by several Task forces, this proves that SCP-XXXX is indeed meant for use in combat scenarios or other such uses, as the horse was not for racing. I currently advise that usage of SCP-XXXX be handled with proper care if it is granted usage.-Sparks</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Addendum XXXX-A-R/R:</strong> Attempted raid and recovery.</p>
<p>On ██/██/████, several Foundation investigative personnel had reported a warehouse that was discovered to have been holding more than 66 instances of SCP-XXXX, almost all of which were in severe condition by a group of urban explorers who had reported it to a local newspaper in [REDACTED]. Foundation agents embedded in the area were able to suppress the report before it could be properly published, with witnesses given Class-A amnestics. Agents were able to locate the warehouse as described by witnesses.</p>
<p>Upon attempting to interact with and contain the SCP-XXXX instances, all of the instances proceed to enter an unstable state and proceed to explode simultaneously. No remains were found afterward. During the event, one agent reported seeing an unusually large horse with red skin in the warehouse during the climax of the event. While an examination of the area did not report a body, a collection of documents was found within a blast resistant safe.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Recovered&nbsp;document</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;document</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Congratulations on purchasing the <span style="text-decoration: underline;">_Defensive Assault Truck</span>_ from Renex Industries, Vehicle &amp; Transportation Division. However, you must sign to agree to the following conditions before we can allow you to own and use our product.<br />
By signing this document, you hereby:</p>
<ul>
<li>Accept full responsibility for any and all damage dealt to passengers, cargo, and self.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Allow for this product to be used for its intended purpose only.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Agree to not tamper with any components that change its main functions
<ul>
<li style="list-style: none; display: inline">
<ul>
<li>Said functions being <span style="text-decoration: underline;">_To terminate hostiles during escort and transportation, or use in assaults or defenses against hostile forces.</span>_</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Accept full responsibility for the care and condition of this product, and accept responsibility for any injuries, dismemberment, death, and any kind of manipulation dealt to the body, mind and/or spirit.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>Agree to terms stating that Arnex Conveyance:V&amp;T, and Renex Industries as a whole is not liable for any of the above conditions being broken, ignored, altered, or contaminated.</li>
</ul>
<p>* If any of the terms above are broken, will agree to return the product or accept the product's self destruct function<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-15" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-15')">15</a></sup>.</p>
<p>PURCHASER’S SIGNATURE<br />
<span style="text-decoration: underline;">_██████</span>___</p>
<p>APPROVAL SIGNATURE</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">_████_<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-16" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-16')">16</a></sup></span></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Attempts to find the listed individuals are currently ongoing, as with attempts to find any other products or locations associated with the company.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Addendum:</strong>Event-XXXX-4-CB<br />
On the 25th of December, ████, SCP-XXXX proceeded to manually activate, emitting sounds resembling grinding metal. SCP-XXXX proceeded to breach containment, killing 3 personnel and causing massive damage to the site at large<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-17" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-17')">17</a></sup> before exiting the main building, eventually leaving the entirety of site-95. Recovery teams eventually located SCP-XXXX in a remote town, causing massive property damage as well as causing, at current estimates, thirty civilian casualties. Recontainment of SCP-XXXX took 5 hours after it had breached containment.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;incident&nbsp;timeline</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Collapse&nbsp;incident&nbsp;timeline</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX enters [REDACTED]</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX process to come to a stop. It remains this way for 2 minutes,</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX proceeds to ram itself into a tall building, causing the structure to collapse on top of it. SCP-XXXX does not seem to be affected in any way.</p>
<p>local law enforcement proceeded to approach SCP-XXXX and open fire on SCP-XXXX once it turned to face them, showing no driver. SCP-XXXX retaliates by opening fire. All of the officers were killed in the ensuing firefight.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX continues to destroy major parts of [REDACTED], killing 5 more civilians.</p>
<p>After demolishing several more buildings in the area, SCP-XXXX proceeds to move to the center of [REDACTED], before SCP-XXXX proceeds to violently skid to a halt, hitting several pedestrians. Said pedestrians were confirmed dead upon impact.SCP-XXXX narrowly avoids hitting an inflatable santa.</p>
<p>Containment teams proceeded to attempt to recontain SCP-XXXX. 15 agents were maimed during the initial recontainment. 2 Helicopters were dispatched to assist with recontainment. MTF-Pi-1 is dispatched to aid in containment.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX proceeds to engage helicopters, eliminating both via the ZPU turret and M6 flamethrower. SCP-XXXX appears to be extremely protective of the inflatable santa.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX evades all containment attempts for the next 13 minutes until a random bullet hits the santa, causing it to slowly deflate.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX ceases movement and all hostilities. At this point, MTF-Epsilon-212 arrives and attempts to use SCP-XXXX-1 to regain control of SCP-XXXX.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX’s hood ornament glows intensly, proceeds to accelerate and rams into the containment truck. SCP-XXXX then attempts to escape. SCP-XXXX-1 is lost for five minutes.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX rams into a blockade, causing Agent ██████ to break his spine, paralyzing him.</p>
<p>Two tanks are deployed to combat SCP-XXXX. During this time SCP-XXXX-1 is retrieved by containment personnel and Agent ██████ is tasked with entering SCP-XXXX and inserting SCP-XXXX-1 into the key slot.</p>
<p>Upon arrival, SCP-XXXX engages both tanks, destroying one of them before being bombarded by artillery. SCP-XXXXs main front guns and turret are destroyed while SCP-XXXX suffers minor harm, having several dents and rust spots covering it, despite the bombardment.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX proceeds to burn several buildings, before ramming itself into the other tank. Bloodstains are visible on the hood of SCP-XXXX.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX proceeds to violently destry several other buildings except those displaying holiday themes. At this time an airstrike was ordered by MTF-Epsilon-212.</p>
<p>Agent ███████ has climbed onto and jumped off of a small building directly onto SCP-XXXX. SCP-XXXX Attempts to remove Agent ███████ by raming itself into several buildings. All remaining tanks and personnel were told to hold fire.</p>
<p>Agent ███████ enters SCP-XXXX, while the SCP attempts to engage all other vehicles in sight. Due to quick thinking by MTF-Epsilon-212 by hastily decorating several vehicles and personnel, no weaponry was used.</p>
<p>Agent ███████’s head hits the steering wheel after SCP-XXXX rams into a non decorated tank, causing him to go unconscious.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-18" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-18')">18</a></sup> SCP-XXXX proceeds to attempt to leave the area. Barricades were put in place to prevent any attempt at further escape.</p>
<p>Agent ███████ recovers after a minute and hastily attempts to insert SCP-XXXX-1 into SCP-XXXX. Agent ███████ successfully inserts SCP-XXXX-1 into SCP-XXXX, subduing the SCP. Agent ███████ is successful in leaving SCP-XXXX so it may be recontained. Agent ████ unintentionally forgets to call off the airstrike.</p>
<p>The airstrike hits SCP-XXXX. Despite being hit with over [REDACTED], SCP-XXXX remained operational, despite being heavily rusted, dented, and burned. Several of the weapons have been destroyed, rendering SCP-XXXX defenceless. MTF-Epsilon-212 proceeds to load SCP-XXXX into a vehicle loader.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX has been successfully recontained. All and all witnesses were given class-B amnestics and MTF-Pi-1 succeeded in creating a cover story of a terrorist attack.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Containment procedures have been revised to accommodate this behavior. While it is currently unknown why or even how SCP-XXXX was able to operate without SCP-XXXX-1, We have speculated that SCP-XXXX may possess some form of autonomy. However that would not explain its escape from the site, specifically built to contain large non sentient movable objects. I recommend we make preparations in the event this does happen again, possibly with modifications to its containment cell. We cannot afford another breach, as the amount of resources and repairs we had to make was well over our annual budget.</p>
<p>-Sparks.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> After another attempted breach a year later, containment procedures have been revised to include this behavior. Further research into this behavior is pending.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Addendum:</strong>After-Incident-Report-XXXX-CB/R</p>
<p>RECOVERED INTELLEGENCE-XXXX-CB/R<br />
After this event, MTF-Epsilon-12 had uncovered a mass production facility in [REDACTED]. Although the facility was in a state of severe neglect, several documents were found detailing the usage and means of production SCP-XXXX underwent. Additionally, an advertisement for SCP-XXXX was found, dating as far back as 1950. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">No explanation for the date, manufacturing, or even potential sales have been found to support the time of print however.</span> G.O.I-XXX Documentation has begun under recent discoveries. View both [DATA EXPUNGED] for more details. A note found on the back was also found, confirming SCP-XXXX may indeed be sentient to a degree.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;recovered&nbsp;advertisement</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Collapse&nbsp;recovered&nbsp;advertisement</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Illegible. Text is covered by a sticker attached reading “Just in time for the holidays!”<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-19" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-19')">19</a></sup></p>
<p>If so, you clearly have not purchased Arnex Convayance's newest line of combat transportation, the D.A.T! That stands for Defensive Assault Trucks people! Not only have we made another vehicle capable of wiping out your neighboring city, but this time it can fend for itself! Watch it fight on its own, tearing through anyone who isn’t its owner! Plus, as an added bonus, this time it can protect its driver!-</p>
<p>Easy to use as 123!</p>
<p>Simply insert the bonded key* and presto! You're ready to claim the roads as your own! Only one signature from one of our five head factories is all that is needed to get one for yourself!**</p>
<p>Don’t Worry folks! We still have our other combat vehicles you just can’t seem to get enough of!</p>
<p>Contact -███-████-████ for more details and get your very own!</p>
<p>[A large image of SCP-XXXX with all of its components armed is shown in the center of the poster. A small family of four are standing next to it, with the youngest hanging from the [REDACTED].</p>
<p>-<span style="font-size:x-small;">All forms and contracts must be signed completely and willingly. Renex Industries is not responsible for any accidents that occur when the product is improperly used. Do not use during the 25th of december.</span></p>
<p>*<span style="font-size:x-small;">If the key is lost/destroyed, contact ███-███-████ for a new one, or for repair. It is advised to stay away from the D.A.T. until representatives arrive.</span></p>
<p>** <span style="font-size:x-small;">Preferably the Vehicle and Transportation Division, although the Assault and Defense Division is also available, as is the Head Division. The Gear and Attire Division along with the Health and Medical Division are last resorts.</span></p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p><span style="font-size:x-small;">Jim, we have a problem.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size:x-small;">You’re whole “Use anything similar to a horse” plan is about to get us all into some deep trouble.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size:x-small;">I would not worry usually but unfortunately the boss is coming by to make sure we make the delivery on time. How do you plan on explaining to him why we started using reindeer instead of the mares?</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size:x-small;">I get trying to find a replacement for the mares is hard, but for god’s sake, we needed those reindeer for the jet sleds! Not this.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size:x-small;">And before you start asking what the big deal is, it's that they won’t start up and act like they’re supposed to. Boss wants these things moving by christmas, but it seems they'll only move DURING christmas. We need them to be ALWAYS active, like an actual animal, not some once a year zombie.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size:x-small;">I don’t know what he’ll think, but odds are once he finds out his rage will be much more desirable than the big boss, which is saying something.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size:x-small;">Also, we lost the one with the glowing red hood ornament. He’s gonna be pissed once he finds out.</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
